WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.765
iOS keyboards can

00:00:01.576 --> 00:00:02.649
now dictate without

00:00:02.461 --> 00:00:03.109
leaving

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.681
KeyboardKit 11.3 adds

00:00:05.493 --> 00:00:07.096
an experimental dictation

00:00:06.908 --> 00:00:08.075
engine that runs

00:00:07.887 --> 00:00:08.877
right inside the

00:00:08.689 --> 00:00:09.880
keyboard extension

00:00:10.092 --> 00:00:10.823
based on a

00:00:10.635 --> 00:00:11.884
workaround Raycast

00:00:11.696 --> 00:00:12.462
discovered

00:00:12.982 --> 00:00:14.232
It records audio

00:00:14.043 --> 00:00:14.998
through an embedded

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:15.882
web view and

00:00:15.824 --> 00:00:16.873
transcribes it with

00:00:16.685 --> 00:00:17.746
the same speech

00:00:17.557 --> 00:00:18.500
recognizer

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:19.453
The main app

00:00:19.359 --> 00:00:20.078
still has to

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:21.057
ask for microphone

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:22.236
permission once and

00:00:22.059 --> 00:00:22.943
Apple could block

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:23.474
the trick

00:00:24.014 --> 00:00:25.134
The release also

00:00:24.946 --> 00:00:25.971
adds actions that

00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:26.985
trigger Shortcuts from

00:00:26.797 --> 00:00:27.610
the keyboard

00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:29.249
cached keyboard previews

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:30.853
and simpler localization

00:00:31.374 --> 00:00:32.388
Full story on

00:00:32.199 --> 00:00:33.095
the dashboard
